{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1085903-virtual-adept-tricks","id":1085903,"title":"Virtual Adept Tricks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-30T14:55:38-07:00","id":1085903,"title":"Virtual Adept Tricks","content":"Just a thread for VA rotes, Wonders, fluff, characters, plots, etc.<br /> <br /> -You know when you try to insert a USB drive but you have it the wrong way so you flip it over, but then the other way is wrong so you flip it over again so it actually goes in? Some VA's will hide sensitive data with a Correspondence effect that operates on the same principle. You have to flip the USB drive in the right ways to access the data.<br /> <br /> -Priorities Sorting Algorithm: using this Time/Entropy rote, a VA can determine what order to perform certain tasks to get the best result. Just enter a list of actions into the program and it will sort them for you. Helpful for planning a busy day, cooking a seven course meal, and figuring out which of the five Technocratic bases you should hack into first.<br /> <br /> -Information Overload: a simple but brutal Mind effect that floods the target's consciousness with input. You know how there are more Youtube videos than any person could watch in their lifetime? Well they all just started playing in your target's head at the same time. This basically stuns them for while, may give them a derangement if they are weak willed.<br /> <br /> -Palette Swap: Forces/Mind effect to make you look like someone else (got the idea from video games like Mortal Kombat where Scorpion, Sub-Zero, Smoke, and several others are the same model with the colors changed).<br /> <br /> -Pac-Man Trap: a Correspondence spell that locks a determined space, like a room or a hallway, into a loop. Try to exit out a door, you find yourself coming in to the same room from a different door. No power pellets unfortunately, but there may be cherries if you look around.<br /> <br /> -Hide a gate to the Digital Web in a fractal code. Only by taking the fractal equation and graphing it out can you enter the DW through this door.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10653-omegaz","name":"OmegaZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10653_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T17:52:30-07:00","id":1085972,"title":"","content":"-Hack The Arm Control Nerve (Life 3/4 or Mind 4): The human body is merely a machine, with its own set of sub-systems devoted to various software processes and hardware tasks. With growing understanding of Life, a hacker can seize control of someone's limbs, either by disrupting nerve paths to forcibly induce muscle spasm, or hack the subconscious mind and load the parts devoted to arm control with junk data. Either method can be used to trip opponents, force items from their grasp, leave them tongue-tied, or merely paralyze them with muscle lock and pain.<br /> <br /> <br /> -Tweak Self Code (Life 3+): Some Virtual Adepts, like the Cyberpunks, work towards transhuman ideals, blending machines and flesh in order to better their bodies. Theirs is a valid method of achieving modifications to the human form, but it is an invasive one, and not the only path. Members of the Reality Hackers, when they are inclined to alter their personal forms, will simply hack their &quot;source code&quot; directly. Not the DNA - although there are VAs who do so - but the metaphysical code that governs their existence within Reality's system. Tweaking values here and there can result in increases to physical (or, with Mind, mental) attributes. Others may blend human data and that of plants and animals, giving them traits of flora and fauna. For those who subscribe to Otherkin ideals, find something fashionable in blending man and animal, or simply recognize the obvious utility of shapeshifting, hacking &quot;source code&quot; is easier than trying to modify DNA or mess around with surgeries or nanomachines. Especially among VAs who don't have backgrounds as biologists or doctors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}